# A/B evidence for the provider-swap work (2026-07-27). It holds REAL customer
# replies harvested read-only from a clone's campaign — company + customer data,
# which the kernel repo must never carry (anti-fork charter §1). Kept on disk so
# the run is reproducible and reviewable; never committed here.
ab/
# Same reason, session-local: the task brief and the A/B report both name
# clones, hosts and absolute paths. They live here for review convenience and
# must never ride into the published repo on a careless `git add .`.
AB-REPORT.md
TASK-multiprovider.md
# Per-session agent memory: one `<session-id>.md` per Claude Code session,
# holding that run's local handoff notes. It is per-machine, per-session state
# — no other machine can use it, and it names clones, hosts and absolute paths,
# which this public repo must never carry (same reason as the entries above).
# Kept on disk so a successor session can read its predecessor.
docs/sessions/
